---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <article class="about">
    <header class="about-header">
      <p class="meta">About</p>
      <h1>The Story So Far</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose drop-cap">
      <p>
        Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. This is where your story goes
        — not a bullet-point resume, but a real narrative. Who you are, what drives you, how
        you got here. Write it like a magazine profile, because that's what this page is.
      </p>

      <p>
        Talk about the things you care about outside of work. The books that shaped your
        thinking, the cities that changed your perspective, the side projects that keep you up
        at night. This is the personal side of the site, and it should feel like sitting down
        for coffee with someone interesting.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm Interested In</h2>

      <p>
        Use this section to talk about your intellectual interests, the problems you find
        fascinating, the communities you're part of. This isn't a skills section — it's a
        window into how you think.
      </p>

      <h2>Outside Work</h2>

      <p>
        Photography, cooking, running, reading, whatever makes you who you are beyond your
        job title. Give people a reason to remember you as a person, not just a professional.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 2rem 6rem;
  }

  .about-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .about-header .meta {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    display: block;
  }

  .about-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  }
</style>
